m/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Found in v4.6.stable.official [89cea1439]\n- Reproducible in v4.6.1.rc1.official [7bfffc846]\n- Not reproducible in v4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbde1]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.rc1 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8228) - AMD Ryzen 5 1500X Quad-Core Processor (8 threads) - 15.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nUpon creating a new `Theme` resource, the \"Default Preview\" tab displays incorrect theme data for properties that haven't been overridden. This seems like a bug as I'd expect the preview to show me what the UI would look like when running the project. Additionally, this doesn't apply to other manually-added preview scenes.\n\n<img width=\"345\" height=\"265\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b942df3b-6a8d-4a59-85de-15bceba32333\" />\n\n<img width=\"401\" height=\"267\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d7b3f67-7d76-4df6-8042-88cf02dafd02\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n 1. Create a new `Theme` resource.\n 2. The \"Default Preview\" tab uses the editor theme settings rather than the actual default theme values.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25195830/issue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https:/